---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base
  title="Protocol map — Codec"
  description="The Codec protocol at a glance: three negotiation pathways (text-tokens, MCP tool-calls with leaf-mode bypass, v0.3 latents) on the same client/gateway/engine triangle, plus v0.4 safety-policy negotiation as a TLS-style capability axis."
>
  <section class="container protocol-map">
    <header class="protocol-map__head">
      <h1>Protocol map</h1>
      <p class="protocol-map__lead">
        Codec runs on one client/gateway/engine triangle. The wire frame, the
        per-modality map, and the response headers shift per pathway — the
        triangle does not. The diagram below is the at-a-glance view; the
        normative spec is in
        <a href="https://github.com/wdunn001/Codec/blob/main/spec/PROTOCOL.md" rel="noopener">PROTOCOL.md</a>
        and pipeline math is in
        <a href="https://github.com/wdunn001/Codec/blob/main/spec/PIPELINES.md" rel="noopener">PIPELINES.md</a>.
      </p>
    </header>

    <figure class="protocol-map__figure">
      <img
        src="/diagrams/protocol-map.svg"
        alt="Codec protocol map showing three pathways: text-tokens (v0.2), MCP tool-calls with leaf-mode bypass, and v0.3 latents. Each pathway shows the client → gateway → engine flow with the wire-level headers and frame types annotated."
      />
      <figcaption>
        Source diagram lives in
        <a href="https://github.com/wdunn001/Codec/blob/main/spec/PROTOCOL.md#negotiation-pathways-at-a-glance" rel="noopener">PROTOCOL.md</a>
        as Mermaid blocks; the polished SVG above is a manual mirror that gets
        updated alongside the spec.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <section class="protocol-map__pathways">
      <article>
        <h2>Text-tokens (v0.2)</h2>
        <p>
          The original wire shape. Engines emit <code>CodecFrame</code>s of
          uint32 token IDs; the gateway forwards them; the client detokenizes
          locally. The <code>Codec-Tokenizer-Map</code> response header carries
          the sha256 of the active tokenizer map so the client can fail fast on
          mismatch.
        </p>
        <p class="protocol-map__where">
          See <a href="/docs/codec-sglang/">codec-sglang</a>,
          <a href="/docs/codec-vllm/">codec-vllm</a>,
          <a href="/docs/codec-llamacpp/">codec-llamacpp</a>.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2>MCP tool-calls (leaf-mode bypass)</h2>
        <p>
          The fast path on a Codec-aware gateway: the tool itself tokenizes its
          result once, against a pinned tokenizer map, and ships the IDs in a
          sibling <code>_codec_meta</code> block. The gateway recognizes the
          pre-tokenized output and bypasses its back-compat shim — the
          <code>[Codec][leaf]</code> log fires; <code>[Codec][shim]</code>
          warnings disappear. Non-Codec-aware tools in the same namespace still
          work via the shim path.
        </p>
        <p class="protocol-map__where">
          See <a href="/docs/codec-metamcp/">codec-metamcp</a>,
          <a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@codecai/mcp-leaf" rel="noopener">@codecai/mcp-leaf</a>,
          <a href="https://hub.docker.com/r/wdunn001/codec-time-leaf" rel="noopener">codec-time-leaf</a> reference image.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2>Latents (v0.3)</h2>
        <p>
          Image and video diffusion models stream VAE latents instead of decoded
          pixels. Wire shape: one <code>LatentStreamHeader</code> followed by
          one or N <code>LatentFrame</code>s per the negotiated pipeline (one
          of seven: <code>raw</code>, <code>int8</code>, <code>int4</code>,
          <code>int8-adaptive</code>, <code>int4-adaptive</code>,
          <code>delta+int8</code>, <code>delta+int4</code>). The client runs
          <code>vae_decode</code> locally; pixels never touch the wire.
        </p>
        <p class="protocol-map__where">
          See <a href="/docs/codec-comfyui/">codec-comfyui</a>,
          <a href="/docs/codec-diffusers/">codec-diffusers</a>,
          <a href="https://github.com/wdunn001/Codec/blob/main/spec/PIPELINES.md" rel="noopener">PIPELINES.md</a>.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2>Safety policies (v0.4)</h2>
        <p>
          A sixth HELLO/READY capability axis. Clients announce
          <code>accept_safety_policies</code> on HELLO; servers respond on READY
          with <code>safety_policy_id</code> + <code>safety_policy_hash</code>.
          The hash anchors to a sanitized descriptor served at
          <code>/.well-known/codec/policies/&lt;id&gt;.json</code> (and the
          content-addressed <code>/sha256/&lt;hex&gt;.json</code> sibling), which
          publishes the <em>shape</em> of enforcement (categories, action types,
          classifier family) but never operator-internal banned-token lists,
          regex patterns, or classifier thresholds. <code>finish_reason:
          "policy_violation"</code> surfaces when a server-side action fires.
          Non-breaking against v0.3 — older clients ignore the new optional
          fields and continue working.
        </p>
        <p class="protocol-map__where">
          See <a href="https://github.com/wdunn001/Codec/blob/main/spec/versions/v0.4.md#safety-policy-negotiation" rel="noopener">spec/versions/v0.4.md</a>,
          <a href="https://github.com/wdunn001/Codec/tree/main/packages/web-safety" rel="noopener">@codecai/web-safety</a> (browser-side prefilter + classifier registry),
          and <a href="https://github.com/wdunn001/codec-supervisor" rel="noopener">codec-supervisor</a> (server-side enforcement + admin app).
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .protocol-map { padding: 3rem 0 5rem; }
  .protocol-map__head { margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .protocol-map__head h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  }
  .protocol-map__lead {
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    max-width: 70ch;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .protocol-map__figure {
    margin: 0 0 3rem;
    background: #0a0d12;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1rem;
  }
  .protocol-map__figure img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
  }
  .protocol-map__figure figcaption {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--fg-faint);
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .protocol-map__pathways {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }
  .protocol-map__pathways article {
    padding: 1.25rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
  }
  .protocol-map__pathways h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  }
  .protocol-map__pathways p {
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  }
  .protocol-map__pathways code {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--data) 15%, transparent);
    color: var(--data);
    padding: 0.0625rem 0.25rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
    font-size: 0.875em;
  }
  .protocol-map__where {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
  }
  .protocol-map__where a { color: var(--fg-muted); }
  .protocol-map__where a:hover { color: var(--fg); }
</style>
